{"schema_version":3,"title":"Active-fire detections per first-level region (ADM1) and month for Southeast Asia (Indonesia, Malaysia, Brunei, Singapore, Thailand, Myanmar, Laos, Cambodia, Vietnam, Philippines, Timor-Leste), MODIS and VIIRS (NASA FIRMS), with a ratio-baseline harmonization","generated":"2026-11-14","units":"detections per region per calendar month (type 0, MODIS confidence >= 30, VIIRS confidence != low)","files":{"regions":"regions.geojson","monthly":"monthly.json","annual":"annual.json","borders":"borders.geojson","outlines":"country-outlines.geojson"},"harmonization":{"method":"province×month ratio baseline","note":"model output will replace this","detail":"VIIRS-equivalent = MODIS x per-province, per-calendar-month VIIRS/MODIS ratio of sums fitted on 2013-2024 for months before VIIRS (2001-01..2012-01, Jan 2012 is a partial VIIRS month); observed VIIRS afterwards. MODIS-equivalent = observed MODIS (MODIS covers every month). Fitted per region; a region with too few MODIS detections in a calendar month uses its country's ratio, and Brunei/Singapore fall back to Malaysia's. Province LOYO error: Indonesia median in loyo_province_median_rel_err; per-country in the series.","loyo_national_monthly_rel_err":0.126,"loyo_province_median_rel_err":0.289,"unreliable_threshold_loyo_rel_err":0.5,"unreliable_note":"series[...].viirs_eq_unreliable = true where the leave-one-year-out relative error of the ratio baseline is >= the threshold: the VIIRS-equivalent estimate there is shown with a warning","label":"Hatched / dashed = <b>estimated</b> (before VIIRS, Jan 2012): MODIS &times; a VIIRS/MODIS ratio fitted on 2013-2024 for each region and calendar month. Where a region has too few detections that month, its country's ratio is used; Brunei and Singapore use Malaysia's. A baseline, not a model. Where the estimate missed by 50 % or more on years it had not seen (Brunei, Singapore and Timor-Leste, and 16 single regions) it is not shown."},"metrics":{"modis_raw":"observed MODIS (Terra+Aqua)","viirs_raw":"observed VIIRS (null before 2012-01)","modis_eq":"MODIS-equivalent, baseline","viirs_eq":"VIIRS-equivalent, baseline (estimated before 2012-02)","modis_clearing":"MODIS detections whose footprint is >= 50 % forest (Hansen tree cover 2000 >= 30 %) lost in the fire year or the next (observed)","viirs_clearing":"same for VIIRS (null before 2012-01)","modis_clearing_to_palm":"of the clearing fires, those where >= half of the lost pixels were planted to oil palm later (Descals planting year in (fire year, 2021]); null for fire years >= 2021","viirs_clearing_to_palm":"same for VIIRS"},"clearing_caveats":["Hansen loss is tree-cover loss and includes plantation harvest and replanting, not only forest clearing.","Timing is by calendar year: a fire in the same year as the loss cannot be ordered before or after the clearing.","Hansen loss runs to 2025: for fire year 2025 only same-year loss exists (flag = 1); for 2024 loss in 2024 and 2025 is used.","MODIS (1 km) misses small fires, so MODIS-era clearing fires are undercounted relative to VIIRS (375 m): compare the two sensors for 2012+.","Peninsular Malaysia and Sabah have old oil-palm and rubber plantations: Hansen loss includes their harvest and replanting, so forest-loss fires there are probably overcounted.","Descals oil-palm tiles are missing over part of the map (about 20 % of Sarawak and large parts of the new countries): 'followed by oil palm' is undercounted there, and a blank is unknown, not zero.","On the mainland, forest-loss fires are probably mostly agricultural burning, not plantation clearing (not measured)."],"sources":"NASA FIRMS archive (MODIS 1 km, VIIRS 375 m); province shapes geoBoundaries gbOpen IDN ADM1 2017, ODbL 1.0, (c) OpenStreetMap contributors, simplified; ADM1 of all other countries: geoBoundaries gbOpen (per-country licences, see credits)","countries":[{"code":"IDN","name":"Indonesia","total":"indonesia","bounds":[94.89,-11.16,141.17,6.06],"viirs_eq_loyo